{"title":"Manim:About","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"border:1px solid black; background:#CEE0F2;text-align:center;\" align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#B0C4DE;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Manim\" title=\"Manim\">Manim</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">About</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Manim:Installation\" title=\"Manim:Installation\">Installation</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Manim:Tutorials\" title=\"Manim:Tutorials\">Tutorials</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://github.com/3b1b/manim\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cf/Manim.png/500px-Manim.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"202\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cf/Manim.png/750px-Manim.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cf/Manim.png/1000px-Manim.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://github.com/3b1b/manim\">Manim</a> is a package written for Python that can be used to produce versatile mathematical animation videos. This is the package used by popular YouTuber <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/3blue1brown\">3Blue1Brown</a> for animating his videos. There are currently two versions of Manim, both open-source.\n</p>\n<ol><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://github.com/3b1b/manim\">Manim</a>, the original version built and maintained by YouTuber <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/3blue1brown\">3Blue1Brown</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://github.com/ManimCommunity/manim/\">Manim Community Edition</a>, a forked version maintained by the open-source community, with verbose documentation and easier installations - This is the version recommended for beginners</li></ol>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Click <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/Manim:Tutorials\">here</a> for some tutorials on how to get started with Manim</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018085849\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 5/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1438/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   33.865      1 Manim\n100.00%   33.865      1 -total\n 51.67%   17.498      1 Template:Manim\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23165:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018085849 and revision id 179480. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}